        {
          "tag": "DIV",
          "text": "",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "DIV",
              "text": "",
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "DIV",
                  "text": "",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "DIV",
                      "text": "Visual Timeline of ST opener included below.",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "list",
                          "ordered": false,
                          "items": [
                            {
                              "text": "While  Exergy is talented over  Inertia, you can simply press  Vengeful Retreat on cooldown while  The Hunt will be providing extra uptime keeping you near 100% uptime with ease.",
                              "nested": null
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "Vengeful Retreat is not on the global cooldown, which is why it allows you to cast it briefly before  Metamorphosis. Used properly, this will cancel the movement of the backflip. If you are struggling to have the movement cancelled by, try using vengeful even earlier before  Metamorphosis.",
                              "nested": null
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "Reaver's Glaive can be cast again in the opener if you generate another cast, however the timing of this is based on RNG of soul fragment spawns.",
                              "nested": null
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "tag": "SPAN",
                          "text": "Aldrachi Reaver",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "DIV",
                      "text": "Visual Timeline of AoE opener included below.",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "list",
                          "ordered": false,
                          "items": [
                            {
                              "text": "The Raid ST build is ONLY recommended for pure single target. Due to  Isolated Prey it loses a significant amount of boss damage as soon as extra targets are introduced.",
                              "nested": null
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "Immolation Aura has a maximum of 5 spell ID's that can be up at once, and  Consuming Fire is limited at 4. This means you should never press more of those buttons consecutively if you get really lucky on procs due to  A Fire Inside.",
                              "nested": null
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "When  Exergy is talented over  Inertia, you can simply press  Vengeful Retreat on cooldown while  The Hunt will be providing extra uptime keeping you near 100% uptime with ease.",
                              "nested": null
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "Fel-Scarred is relatively simple in that there isn’t much room to swap around talents. This means that your opener will usually stay the same, regardless of what build you’re running with this Hero Talent.",
                              "nested": null
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "It is relatively easy to forget the first  Annihilation cast after the first  Eye Beam in the combo, however not casting this Annihilation before casting  Metamorphosis will cost you a  Demonsurge and must be avoided.",
                              "nested": null
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "In AoE Builds  Screaming Brutality will now apply  Burning Wound automatically making it a non-issue. This is also why in AoE there is a raw  Blade Dance early in the combo.",
                              "nested": null
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "tag": "SPAN",
                          "text": "Fel-Scarred",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
